WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.960
His ace monster has appeared.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.460
It has more ATK than Playmaker’s monster.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.660
Yeah.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:18.960
Due to Crystal Heart's effect, 
King T Wrextle gains 600 ATK!

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.730
Then I summon Dinowrestler Valeonyx!

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:32.300
When this card is summoned, it activates 
its effect on a Dinowrestler Link Monster!

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.660
The target is King T Wrextle!

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.920
I set one card.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.160
Battle!

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.130
King T Wrextle attacks Storm Cipher!

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:50.970
Due to World Dino Wrestling’s 
effect, King T Wrextle gains 200 ATK!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.450
Crazy Evolution’s effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:05.200
When the Storm Cipher that was 
affected by this card is destroyed...

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.290
...I banish this card to draw a card!

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.220
I end my turn.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.490
Hey!  That Crystal Heart belongs to Earth!

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.370
Take care of it until we get it back!

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.730
Ya hear me?

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:25.960
You cannot defeat me.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:48.300
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:55.090
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:02.410
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:08.980
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:15.730
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:22.960
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:29.670
I want to share your pain

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.970
Go Onizuka and the AI’s 
synchronicity is increasing.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:24.530
I'm almost there.  To 
becoming a perfect duelist.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:29.800
Playmaker, you seem unsure whether 
to defeat Go Onizuka or not.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.660
But this is revenge for Earth!

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:40.410
No matter how you feel about him, he’s 
only thinking about crushing you- crushing us.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.340
I know.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.930
It’s my turn!  I draw!

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.450
I summon Dotscaper!

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:55.250
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.310
Link Summon!

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.060
Link 1 Linkuriboh!

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.530
Dotscaper’s effect activates!

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:09.010
When it's sent to the graveyard, 
it Special Summons itself!

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.450
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.850
The summoning conditions are two monsters!

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.320
Link Summon!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.280
Link 2 Security Dragon!

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:28.380
Security Dragon’s effect activates!

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:34.620
When it's co-linked, it can return 
one of your monsters to your hand!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.100
Go home, T Wrextle!

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.520
But Valeonyx’s effect.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:50.980
King T Wrextle isn’t affected by monsters 
that have equal or fewer Link Markers.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.320
What?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:05:00.160
This is Valeonyx’s effect 
that activated last turn.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.610
Link 3 or lower monsters' effects 
are useless against King T Wrextle.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:10.970
But if a monster is Link 4, it'll affect it.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:16.970
When I have at least two Link Monsters on 
my field, I can Special Summon Cross Debug!

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:23.410
Appear for a third time!  The 
circuit that leads to the future!

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:30.650
I set Linkslayer, Cross Debug and Link 
2 Security Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.120
Link Summon!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.760
Appear, Link 4 Firewall Dragon!

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.020
Firewall Dragon’s effect activates!

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.640
It returns monsters to the hand, up to the 
number of monsters co-linked to Firewall Dragon!

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.960
Emergency Escape!

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:54.480
King T Wrextle, thanks for your time.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.170
Everything you do is within expectations.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.920
I activate the trap card, Dino Deceit!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.780
If your monster with equal 
or more Link Markers than a

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.520
Dinowrestler Link Monster 
activates an effect...

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.690
...all monsters on your field 
have their effects negated.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.660
Negated again?

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:21.400
Then I can set a spell or 
trap card from my hand.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:27.100
And you must battle this turn!

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:32.850
When Go Onizuka starts a battle, he 
can use King T Wrextle's effect...

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.130
...to choose which monster 
Playmaker attacks with.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:40.850
Right now, Playmaker can 
only attack King T Wrextle.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:45.170
If you don’t attack with 
the monster I select...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:49.080
...that monster will be destroyed 
at the end of battle.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.560
I select Firewall Dragon.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.860
As expected.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.570
But we can’t attack in this situation.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.540
What should we do?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:05.280
Will you attack?  Or…

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:13.220
So you won’t attack.  Then it’s gone.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.260
Damn.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.860
I end my turn.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.660
In the end, we couldn’t do anything!

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:26.380
A duelist that fused human 
intellect with AI thinking.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.480
Go Onizuka’s dueling has 
entered unknown territory.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:37.140
But to defeat Playmaker, Go Onizuka 
still must duel beyond expectations.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:40.490
My turn.  I draw.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:43.140
I'll end you this turn.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.920
I set one card.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.160
I activate the Continuous Trap, Dino Domain!

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.140
I return a Dinowrestler 
on my field to my hand.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.660
I return…

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.570
King T Wrextle!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:04.200
Huh?  He wouldn't let us return his 
monster, but he did it himself.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:11.380
Due to Dino Domain, your monsters can't 
affect my monsters until the end of this turn.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.610
And when I have my monster 
in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:20.090
...Dino Domain can’t be targeted 
by effects nor destroyed!

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:24.290
Now effects can't affect 
Go Onizuka’s monsters.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:30.190
Playmaker only has Linkuriboh 
with its effects negated.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:35.440
Was that worth returning 
his ace monster, T Wrextle?

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:38.430
He has Crystal Heart.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.790
Due to Crystal Heart’s 
effect, I Special  Summon

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.100
Dinowrestler Terra Parkourio 
from the graveyard!

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:50.610
Then I place a G Golem 
Counter on Crystal Heart.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:57.060
For every G Golem Counter, it gains 600 ATK!

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:00.850
Appear!  The circuit to victory!

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:03.860
Link Summon!

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:09.200
Appear again, Link 3 King T Wrextle!

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.400
Due to Terra Parkourio’s 
effect from the graveyard...

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:19.880
...Valeonyx is Special Summoned from the 
graveyard in defense position by negating its effects!

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:24.210
King T Wrextle is once again 
next to Crystal Heart’s link.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:33.630
Due to Crystal Heart’s effect, King T 
Wrextle gains 600 ATK for every G Golem Counter.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:39.600
Playmaker, I’m ending this.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:45.970
At this rate, Go Onizuka 
is in physical danger!

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:47.860
Log him out by force!

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.340
B-But…

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.010
He can't take it anymore!

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:53.710
I told you not to butt in!

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:56.210
If you can’t, leave!

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:58.180
Battle!

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:02.930
King T Wrextle attacks Linkuriboh!

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:07.650
Due to World Dino Wrestling’s 
effect, it gains 200 ATK!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:10.620
Cross Debug’s effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:15.870
I banish this card and select Firewall 
Dragon in the graveyard as the target!

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.980
Now Linkuriboh can’t 
be destroyed in battle,

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:23.900
and it gains ATK equal to 
Firewall Dragon’s ATK!

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.420
But you still take damage.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.890
Good.  This is fine.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:51.810
The more you fight back, the 
greater heights I reach.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.970
I end my turn.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.100
He managed to survive.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.850
But he’s surrounded on all sides.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:06.960
No matter what Playmaker 
does, next turn will be…

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:09.060
We have 1000 LP left.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.570
That means we can activate our Skill, but...

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:17.520
Show how you struggle pathetically.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.930
It may be pathetic, but I 
won’t give up until the end!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:25.490
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:36.820
Playmaker…  Don't tell me you're…

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.920
Yeah.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:42.320
Seriously?  But Go Onizuka has Anti Skill!

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.370
Are you desperate?

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:47.890
I bet on my instincts!

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:51.020
Instincts?  Seriously?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.910
Instincts?

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:56.500
Relying on instincts means 
you’ve fallen, Playmaker.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:00.740
You're one to talk!  You're all instinct!

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:05.210
That’s why I gave that 
up and fused with an AI.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:07.710
Let's go!

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.780
Let's be desperate!

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.780
Pointless.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:24.250
I activate my Skill, Neo Storm Access!

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:27.960
Once per duel, I can negate your Skill!

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.030
I activate my Skill, Anti Skill!

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.180
Damn!

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.140
Then I draw two cards.

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:47.620
It's over, Playmaker.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:51.090
No.  I was waiting for this moment!

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:52.060
What?

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:55.530
I activate the trap card, Draw Discharge!

00:12:55.530 --> 00:13:01.580
When you draw other than during the Draw 
Phase, if there are monster cards among them...

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:08.250
...you take damage equal to their total ATK, 
and all the cards you drew are banished!

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:12.940
You forced me to use Anti 
Skill so you could counter it.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.080
Nice, Playmaker!

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:21.420
If both the cards you drew 
are high ATK monsters...

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:24.480
...you lose, Go Onizuka!

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.620
Well done, Playmaker.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:33.510
The cards I drew are Dinowrestlers 
with 1800 and 2600 ATK.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:37.080
That totals 4400!

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.760
We win!  Go Onizuka’s LP are-

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.710
No.  You’re finished!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:44.670
What?

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.910
I activate the Counter Trap, Dino Sense!

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:55.280
When there’s a Dinowrestler Link Monster 
on my field and you activate a trap card...

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:58.260
...it's negated and banished!

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:05.230
And you take 300 damage for 
every monster on my field!

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:08.700
You take 900 damage!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.620
Playmaker!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:28.900
I expected you'd try something 
against my Anti Skill.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.890
There's nothing left you can do.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:39.260
He dodged his comeback attempt.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:40.860
Playmaker…

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:45.570
No way…  Playmaker is going to lose.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.210
It’s a hopeless situation.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.430
The wind?

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:03.700
What is it?

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.860
Nice, Playmaker!

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:10.250
Your instincts really created a miracle!

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.820
What do you mean?

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:14.000
It’s not over yet!

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:17.300
A miraculous storm is about to blow!

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:25.470
Neo Storm Access had another effect!

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:30.440
When you have 100 or less LP, and your Skill 
didn’t add a new card to your Extra Deck...

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:35.820
...you can add a random Cyberse in 
the Data Storm to your Extra Deck!

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:38.920
Then you draw a card from your deck!

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.970
Risk your life to achieve success.

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:58.290
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.110
Neo Storm Access!

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.020
Then I draw!

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:26.740
You only have 100 LP!

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:30.710
I'll crush your miracle and end you!

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.910
I summon Firewall Guardian!

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:39.680
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:44.100
I set Firewall Guardian and 
Linkuriboh in the Link Markers!

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.020
Link Summon!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:51.090
Appear, Link 2 Clock Lizard!

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:55.460
Firewall Guardian’s effect activates!

00:16:55.460 --> 00:17:00.590
When it's used to Link Summon, it Special 
Summons itself from the graveyard!

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:05.670
And when there’s a Field Spell, 
I can Special Summon Grid Sweeper!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:12.150
I overlay Level 4 Firewall 
Guardian and Grid Sweeper!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:19.800
What’s that?

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.390
Not a Link Summon?

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:25.620
With these two monsters, I 
build the Overlay Network!

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:35.690
The wall of power that 
annihilates everything!

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:39.760
Manifest as the dragon’s fang!

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.860
Xyz Summon!

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:51.850
Appear, Rank 4 Firewall Xyz Dragon!

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.670
Xyz Summon?

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.100
Xyz Dragon’s effect activates!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:14.580
I use two Overlay Units to Special Summon a 
Link 4 Cyberse from my graveyard next to its link!

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:17.490
Come, Firewall Dragon!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:27.360
And Xyz Dragon gains 500 ATK for every Link 
Marker that the monsters it's linked to have!

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.590
Firewall is Link 4!

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:31.830
Clock Lizard is Link 2!

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:35.070
Therefore, it gains 3000!

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:38.200
Firewall Dragon’s effect activates!

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.610
Emeregency Escape!

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:43.840
We return King T Wrextle to your hand!

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:46.310
Dino Domain’s effect activates!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:49.040
By returning a Dinowrestler to my hand...

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:54.660
...my monsters aren’t affected by your 
monsters' effects until the end of the turn!

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:57.170
I return Valeonyx to the hand.

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:01.190
I activate Grid Sweeper’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.420
I banish this card and Clock Lizard!

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:08.600
Then I destroy one of your cards!

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:12.840
But my monsters aren’t affected 
by your monsters’ effects!

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:15.810
My target is World Dino Wrestling!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:21.800
Now I can attack with two of my monsters!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.940
Battle!

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:25.940
At this moment, King T Wrextle’s effect!

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:29.520
I’ll have Firewall Dragon attack first!

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:33.490
Firewall Dragon has 2500 ATK.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:36.260
If it attacks, you’ll run out of LP.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:38.300
So you can’t attack.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.260
Damn!  Not again!

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:41.060
Wrong!

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:45.970
Firewall Dragon attacks King T Wrextle!

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:48.780
No!

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:51.010
You want to self-destruct, Playmaker?

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.470
Firewall Guardian’s effect 
activates from my graveyard!

00:19:54.470 --> 00:20:01.930
When I declare an attack, I banish it from my 
graveyard to negate Firewall Dragon’s attack!

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:07.160
Then your monster can only be affected by 
its own effects until the end of this turn.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:10.120
And its ATK become 0!

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:14.100
0 ATK…

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:18.100
Even God or Ai couldn’t 
have anticipated this.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:23.400
Firewall Xyz Dragon attacks King T Wrextle!

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:28.280
Rising Crypt Limit!

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:54.330
Playmaker…

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:00.430
C'mon!  Log him out now!

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:03.650
No!  Activate the capture unit!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:07.950
I'm taking back Earth’s data!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.690
What’s this?

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:20.160
He logged out?

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:24.480
Zaizen!  What are you doing?

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:28.060
Do you want to make us murderers?

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:35.000
This is...

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.790
We only managed to get that back.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:39.470
Aqua, hold on to it.

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:42.480
That'd make Earth the happiest.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:43.710
Ai…

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:47.680
Now Earth will rest more easy.

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:51.630
I wonder if Go Onizuka is okay.

00:21:51.630 --> 00:21:56.650
He might also be a victim of this battle.

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:59.660
We can’t waste time.

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:03.110
We have to end this fight quickly.

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.730
Trapped in conventionality

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:25.170
